Requirements:

- at most `concurrency` children alive at once, reports in input order;
- stdout is split into lines as it arrives, `onLine` is called per line
  tagged with the job id, and every line is also collected into
  `report.lines` — including the last line when it has no trailing newline;
- each job gets the two-stage timeout from ex3, and a timed-out job still
  reports the lines it produced before it was killed;
- a spawn failure produces a report with `error` set and does not stop the
  batch;
- `active()` returns how many children are currently running.

