## Problem 6 — a cache that cannot leak

Edit `ex6/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export interface LruCache<V> {
  get(key: string): V | undefined;
  set(key: string, value: V): void;
  delete(key: string): boolean;
  readonly size: number;
  readonly bytes: number;
}

export function createLruCache<V>(options: {
  maxBytes: number;
  sizeOf: (value: V) => number;
}): LruCache<V>
```

Least-recently-used eviction with an exact byte budget:

- `get` counts as a use and moves the key to the most-recent end;
- `set` on an existing key replaces the value and **subtracts the old size
  before adding the new one**;
- after any `set`, evict from the least-recent end until `bytes <= maxBytes`;
- a single value larger than `maxBytes` is not stored at all (and evicts
  nothing);
- `bytes` is always exactly the sum of `sizeOf` over the stored values.

```ts
const c = createLruCache<string>({ maxBytes: 10, sizeOf: (v) => v.length });
c.set("a", "12345");
c.set("b", "12345");
c.get("a");
c.set("c", "1");      // evicts "b", the least recently used
c.size;               // 2
```

