## Problem 7 — subscriptions that go away

Edit `ex7/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export interface Registry<T> {
  subscribe(subscriber: object, handler: (event: T) => void, meta?: unknown): () => void;
  publish(event: T): number;             // returns how many handlers ran
  metaFor(subscriber: object): unknown;  // from a WeakMap
  readonly size: number;
}

export function createRegistry<T>(): Registry<T>
```

Rules:

- `subscribe` returns an unsubscribe function; calling it twice is safe and
  only removes once;
- `size` is exactly the number of live subscriptions, so a test that
  subscribes and unsubscribes 1,000 times ends at 0;
- the same `subscriber` object may subscribe more than once, and each
  subscription unsubscribes independently;
- `meta` is stored in a `WeakMap` keyed by the subscriber, so it does not keep
  the subscriber alive;
- a handler that throws must not stop the other handlers, and `publish` still
  returns the number that ran.

```ts
const r = createRegistry<number>();
const off = r.subscribe(obj, (n) => seen.push(n), { name: "obj" });
r.publish(1);        // 1
off(); off();
r.size;              // 0
```

