## Problem 8 — is this a leak?

Edit `ex8/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export type Trend = "stable" | "sawtooth" | "growing" | "insufficient-data";

export function classifyTrend(
  samples: readonly number[],
  options?: { windowSize?: number; growthThreshold?: number },
): { trend: Trend; minima: number[]; slopePerWindow: number }
```

`samples` are `heapUsed` readings at a fixed interval. Analyse the **minima**,
not the raw series:

1. split the samples into consecutive windows of `windowSize` (default 5) and
   take the minimum of each — this approximates "what survived the last
   collection";
2. fit a least-squares line through the minima (x = window index) to get
   `slopePerWindow`;
3. fewer than three complete windows → `"insufficient-data"`;
4. `slopePerWindow` greater than `growthThreshold` (default: 1% of the first
   minimum, per window) → `"growing"`;
5. otherwise, `"sawtooth"` if the raw series varies by more than 10% of its
   own minimum, and `"stable"` if it does not.

```ts
classifyTrend([100, 180, 105, 190, 102,  101, 185, 103, 188, 100]);
// { trend: "sawtooth", ... }   // peaks vary, minima do not
```

