Edit `ex4/solution.ts`. Implement:

```ts
export function foldStacks(
  profile: { nodes: Array<{ id: number; callFrame: { functionName: string }; hitCount?: number; children?: number[] }> },
): string[]
```

Produce the input format flame-graph renderers consume: one line per stack
that has samples, of the form `frame;frame;frame count`.

- the frame name is `functionName`, or `(anonymous)` when empty;
- a node's count is its **own** `hitCount`, not its subtree's — the renderer
  sums children itself, and using the subtree makes every box as wide as the
  root;
- nodes with zero hits produce no line;
- identical stacks are merged, summing their counts (the same stack can appear
  more than once when a profile has been concatenated);
- output is sorted by stack string ascending, so the file is stable across
  runs and diffable.

```ts
foldStacks(profile);
// [ "(root);main;parseRow 412", "(root);main;parseRow;trim 88" ]
```

```
